# $cond skips evaluation of earlier branches' value when condition is false,
# and correctly evaluates the first matching branch's value.
# Distinct from cond_unused_branch_error: tests the false-then-true path,
# not that an error in a later branch is skipped.
[cond [[false [error "first branch is false, value must not be forced"]] [true "second"]]]
===
String("second")
